    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2310.03744_rag::chunk_001</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MLLMs that process inputs from diverse modalities and solely generate outputs in text format</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The recent development of MLLM posts a strong need for moderni</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The training process of MLLMs, as continued learning on newly introduced visual features</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MLLMs involve a complex training and evaluation pipeline with numerous design decisions to consider.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">POPE is a benchmark for evaluating object hallucination in MLLMs</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">evaluate hallucinations in MLLMs</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">greatly compressing the token sequence for MLLM.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">it still remains unclear what the best recipe is to train LMMs towards the goal of general-purpose assistants.</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
